n who brought peace to the  multiverse this is not the same king  that we are going to be meeting the one  that we're going to meet in ant-man 3 is  going to be the true villain and from  what i've heard there are actually going  to be a few different variants of king  the cockerer who are going to be the  main villains so our heroes the avengers  doctor strange all of these other ones  that haven't really come together yet  they're not just going to have to deal  with one king but they're going to have  to deal with multiple kangs and the  kangs will probably fight each other as  well kind of going by the original story  of the original multiversal war where  the kangs tried to dominate the  multiverse we can assume that the same  thing will probably happen here a bunch  of different kings will show up trying  to take over the universe so our heroes  are going to run into multiple variants  of king all of which are trying to take  over the universe but i would like to  think that the main villain of this  secret war storyline that is going to  happen in the mcu well that's already  happening in the mcu is going to be  actually our universe's version of kang  the conqueror nathaniel richards now  nathaniel richards technically should  not be born yet he is born way into the  future but in the future he comes across  a time traveling machine and manages to  go back in time all the way back to  ancient egyptian times and he becomes  the pharaoh rama tut in fact in moon  night we got actual easter eggs for kang  the conqueror as ramatu and these were  confirmed to be actual easter eggs so  kang is here he's in our universe but  he's most likely right now in the  quantum realm which is why ant-man and  the wasp quantum mania is going to be  the real film to bring kang into the mcu  now this is all really really exciting  and if you think it is exciting well  guess what it's actually going to get  even more exciting because i believe  that while all of this is happening 